      "title": "Third quarter 2026 earnings: EPS and revenues miss analyst expectations",
      "body": "Third quarter 2026 results: EPS: ₹2.33 (down from ₹2.63 in 3Q 2025). Revenue: ₹30.1b (up 1.3% from 3Q 2025). Net income: ₹2.71b (down 8.1% from 3Q 2025). Profit margin: 9.0% (in line with 3Q 2025). Revenue missed analyst estimates by 2.5%. Earnings per share (EPS) also missed analyst estimates by 2.9%. Revenue is forecast to grow 8.6% p.a. on average during the next 3 years, compared to a 13% growth forecast for the Chemicals industry in India. Over the last 3 years on average, earnings per share has increased by 7% per year but the company’s share price has remained flat, which means it is significantly lagging earnings.",
